{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Baseline maintenance step required in this change (verified on origin/main): `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py::test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree` asserts `set(baseline) | admitted == live`, so removing the 13 `REBAR_LLM_OVERLAP_*` env vars and the `[llm] overlap_*` keys leaves stale rows that `scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` tolerates but the pytest does not. Run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` after the removal and commit the resulting `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (it refuses while `new>0`, so it cannot bless a regression). Precedent: commit 81da792 dropped `env_var::REBAR_HLC` the same way. This is the operator-sanctioned path for this epic, superseding the \"do not hand-edit\" instruction in the description for this file only; `.github/complexity-baseline.json` is still not hand-edited (its stale entry passes both the script and its test)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788805893200412456,"uuid":"ee32923f-a017-428c-9bef-2d3a9373b478"}